<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('partials/head') %>
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('partials/nav') %>

  <main class="page">
    <div class="chapter">
      <span class="chapter__numeral">I.</span>
      <span class="chapter__title">Home</span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="title"><%= site.name %></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      <%= site.role %>. Before coding, I kept the hardware running — now I bring the same
      habit of tracing a problem to its root cause into building software.
    </p>

    <dl class="facts">
      <div>
        <dt>Based in</dt>
        <dd><%= site.location %></dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Looking for</dt>
        <dd>Junior developer roles</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Background</dt>
        <dd>Assistant Field Service Technician</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="/systems" class="btn btn--primary">View systems developed</a>
      <a href="/cv" class="btn btn--ghost">Read my CV</a>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"><span class="divider__mark">&#10022;</span></div>

    <p style="font-size: 1rem;">
      I spent my early career fixing and maintaining physical equipment — the kind of work
      where you can't guess, you have to isolate the fault and prove it. After finishing my
      degree, I've been applying that same discipline to writing software: reading
      documentation closely, testing assumptions, and building things that hold up outside
      a demo.
    </p>

    <p class="pull-quote">
      I'd rather understand <span>why</span> something works than memorize what it does.
    </p>

    <div class="divider divider--label"><h2>Skills</h2></div>
    <dl class="ledger">
      <div class="ledger__row">
        <dt>Languages</dt>
        <dd>JavaScript, Node.js, Python, HTML/CSS, SQL</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger__row">
        <dt>Tools &amp; platforms</dt>
        <dd>Express, Git/GitHub, Vercel, VS Code</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger__row">
        <dt>Hardware &amp; field work</dt>
        <dd>Diagnostics, soldering/rework, cabling &amp; networking, multimeter/oscilloscope</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger__row">
        <dt>Working style</dt>
        <dd>Root-cause debugging, documentation, on-site troubleshooting</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </main>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
